    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Reproduce first (fail-before):
      - a jest test: in the saved state, the attachments are not listed, and an attachments-only Save sends no target;
      - a BFF test: a save naming unsaved attachments for an already-saved email, where no Completed job exists under the same key, creates no children today.</step>
    <step>Server: the additive saved-attachment names on the identity response; the explicit add-attachments save that does not need a prior job. ADR-008 A1 treatment if the service finds the document itself.</step>
    <step>Pane: the compact saved section (owner points 1–3, 9), the Profile changes (points 5–6), the attachments list with saved checks and unsaved checkboxes (point 7), and Save only when something is unsaved (point 8). After a successful add, the list shows the new ones as saved.</step>
    <step>Gates:
      - BFF: build with 0 warnings; the affected test classes; ArchTests (full).
      - office-addins: jest (all suites), tsc (68-error baseline, none in changed files), ESLint and Prettier, webpack production build with the CI env.
      - Publish delta and vulnerable packages.
      - List the new test files for the gate list.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A saved email shows ONE top section: "Saved to Spaarke", the email subject, sender and date, "Filed to {record name} ({record number})" with an icon-only open-record link, and icon-only View Document and Copy Link buttons with tooltips. There is no separate "Email" header and no separate "Filed to" card.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With any unsaved attachment, the top section shows a warning triangle and "Unsaved attachments". With none, there is no warning.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The attachments list shows each attachment with a saved check, or with a checkbox if it is not saved. The Save button appears only when at least one attachment is unsaved, and is enabled only when at least one unsaved one is ticked.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Save sends the add-attachments request for exactly the ticked names. The server creates exactly those children under the existing .eml, filed like it, with NO new .eml and no re-upload, even when no prior job exists for this user and key. Afterwards the list shows them as saved and the warning clears when none are left.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative:
      - the caller without the required right on the saved .eml (or its record) gets no children, a clear refusal, and the .eml unchanged;
      - a name the stored .eml does not hold is reported as not stored, never created from request bytes;
      - an already saved name is never created twice.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The identity response's saved-attachment names are additive. An older pane is unaffected, and a failed child read leaves the field absent. The pane then shows the attachments without saved marks, and keeps today's behaviour, without claiming they are unsaved.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Profile:
      - no "Document type" row for an email (kept for Word);
      - Generate Profile / Refresh is an icon-only button with a tooltip at the right of the "Profile" label, in both modes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">"Save again as a new document" still saves a new document; Word's saved view and version saves keep working.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <justification>
    <existing>The identity response (`resolve-email-identity`), the Office save route, task 138's `EmailAttachmentAddPlanner`, and SaveFlow's saved state.</existing>
    <extension>Extends them: an additive response field, an additive request field on the existing save route, and the planner's own child read and name rule. No new route, column or service unless shown necessary.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A user cannot add the attachments they skipped the first time: the only path today silently saves nothing. They cannot see which attachments are saved, so they re-save the email or give up.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <notes></notes>
  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
